#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:3
msgid "Pin packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:5
msgid ""
"Hold an installation at its current version so upgrade and reinstall skip it "
"until you unpin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:9
msgid "Pin it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:11
msgid "$ pipx pin black"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:15
msgid ""
"Pinned environments are skipped by ``pipx upgrade``, ``pipx upgrade-all``, "
"and ``pipx reinstall``, so the app and its dependencies keep their versions "
"until you unpin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:18
msgid ""
"``pipx pin PACKAGE`` pins the main package and any injected packages in that "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:19
msgid ""
"``pipx pin PACKAGE --injected-only`` leaves the main package upgradable but "
"pins every injected package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:20
msgid ""
"``pipx pin PACKAGE --skip PKG_A PKG_B`` pins injected packages except the "
"listed ones (implies ``--injected-only``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:21
msgid ""
"``pipx unpin PACKAGE`` re-enables upgrades for the package and anything "
"pinned with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:23
msgid ""
"Pass ``--output json`` to read the changed and skipped packages from a "
"script, or ``--quiet`` to omit confirmations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:27
msgid ""
"pipx pins the main package and injected packages, not individual transitive "
"dependencies. Pinning the main package freezes its whole dependency set, "
"because pipx skips ``pip install --upgrade`` for that environment. For how "
"pipx records this metadata, see :doc:`../explanation/how-pipx-works`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:33
msgid "Verify it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:35
msgid "$ pipx list --pinned"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/pin-packages.rst:39
msgid "Add ``--include-injected`` to also list pinned injected packages."
msgstr ""
